  "title": "Alisher Navoi's Khamsa",
  "summary": "Alisher Navoi wrote his Khamsa, a cycle of five poems, between 1483 and 1485, mostly in Chagatai. It comprises Hayrat al-Abrar, Farhad and Shirin, Layli and Majnun, Sab'ai Sayyar and Saddi Iskandari. Sources describe it as the first work of the Khamsa genre composed in a Turkic language.",
